  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an array AAA containing NNN positive integers.\n\nA subsequence of this array is called cool if the averages of all non-empty subsequences of this subsequence are present in the complement subsequence.  The complement subsequence refers to the subsequence formed by the elements we didn't consider.\n\nFor example, consider the array A=[8,4,2,1,3,2,5,8,2]A=[8, 4, 2, 1, 3, 2, 5, 8, 2]A=[8,4,2,1,3,2,5,8,2].\n\n\nConsider the subsequence [2,2,8][2, 2, 8][2,2,8] of this array.\n\nThe complement subsequence is [8,4,1,3,5,2][8, 4, 1, 3, 5, 2][8,4,1,3,5,2].\n\nThe non-empty subsequences of [2,2,8][2, 2, 8][2,2,8] are [2],[8],[2,2],[2,8],[2,2,8][2], [8], [2, 2], [2, 8], [2, 2, 8][2],[8],[2,2],[2,8],[2,2,8], with averages 2,8,2,5,42, 8, 2, 5, 42,8,2,5,4 respectively.\nAll of these values are present in the complement subsequence, therefore [2,2,8][2, 2, 8][2,2,8] is a cool subsequence.\n\n\nNote that **no rounding is done when computing the average.** For example the average of {1,2,5}\\{1, 2, 5\\}{1,2,5} is 1+2+53=83\\frac{1+2+5}{3} = \\frac{8}{3}31+2+5​=38​, we do not round it to 222 or 333.\n\nFind **any** cool subsequence of the array with length at least 111, or report that no such subsequence exists.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN — the length of the array.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ — the elements of the array.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case,\n\n\n\nIf a cool subsequence exists in AAA, print two lines.\n\nThe first line should contain an integer KKK (1≤K&lt;N1 \\leq K \\lt N1≤K&lt;N), denoting the length of the cool subsequence you found.\nThe second line should contain KKK space-separated integers denoting the elements of the cool subsequence.\n\n\nIf no cool subsequence exists, print the single integer −1-1−1 on a new line instead.\n\nIf there are multiple cool subsequences in AAA, any of them will be accepted as a valid output.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\leq T \\leq 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤2⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^51≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤Ai≤1071 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^71≤Ai​≤107",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
